@page "/"
@* Page/container — orchestrates the route only, no UI logic, no direct use of base components,
   per the-standard-architecture's UI rules ("Pages are route containers and do not require
   business logic"). All actual call-screen UI lives in the CallScreen Core Component.
   @rendermode InteractiveServer: CallScreen needs live interactivity (button clicks, the
   once-a-second call timer, call-event subscriptions) — without this the page renders once,
   statically, with no server-side event wiring at all. *@
@using Ringly.Samples.BlazorServer.Components.Cores
@rendermode InteractiveServer

<PageTitle>Ringly — Blazor Server</PageTitle>

<CallScreen />
<DepartmentsPanel />
<SupportPanel />
<AgentConsole />
